&lt;p>&lt;strong>User Query&lt;/strong>: The process begins when a user submits a question or query to the system.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Logging Handler Service</title><link>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/logging-handler-service/</link><pubDate>Fri, 04 Apr 2025 11:24:04 +0530</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/logging-handler-service/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Chunking Strategy</title><link>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/chunking-strategy/</link><pubDate>Fri, 04 Apr 2025 11:23:46 +0530</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/chunking-strategy/</guid><description>&lt;p>We tried 2 chunking strategies:&lt;/p>
&lt;ol>
&lt;li>Semantic chunking&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Token based chunking&lt;/li>
&lt;/ol>
&lt;p>Semantic chunking did not give expected results, so we are now using token based.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 class="relative group">Token based chunking strategy:
&lt;div id="token-based-chunking-strategy" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700"
style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#token-based-chunking-strategy" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Token-based chunking is our current approach for processing legislation documents. Here&amp;rsquo;s how the process works:&lt;/p>
&lt;ol>
&lt;li>
&lt;p>&lt;strong>Document Collection and Conversion&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Receive legislation documents from clients in PDF format&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Store in a dedicated folder with meaningful filenames&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Track file hashes to identify duplicate documents&lt;/li>
&lt;li>If a PDF with a specific hash is already processed, only the new file path is appended in file_hash.json
&lt;strong>For LIs (Legal Instruments)&lt;/strong>&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Use &lt;strong>pymupdf4llm&lt;/strong> conversion method&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Command: &lt;code>python -m ragcore.markdown_chunking.create_markdown &amp;lt;pdf_data_base&amp;gt; &amp;lt;markdown_data_dir&amp;gt; --pattern &amp;quot;**/legislation/LIs/*.pdf&amp;quot;&lt;/code>&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>&lt;strong>For Acts and Regulations&lt;/strong>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Filehash JSON structure</title><link>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/filehash-json-structure/</link><pubDate>Fri, 04 Apr 2025 10:18:35 +0530</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/filehash-json-structure/</guid><description>&lt;p>This file is used to store and identify duplicate files in dataset.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 class="relative group">Structure
&lt;div id="structure" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700"
style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#structure" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-json" data-lang="json">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>{
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#f92672">&amp;#34;&amp;lt;sha256_file_hash&amp;gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span>: [
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;&amp;lt;file_1&amp;gt;.pdf&amp;#34;&lt;/span>,
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#e6db74">&amp;#34;&amp;lt;file_2&amp;gt;.pdf&amp;#34;&lt;/span>,
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010">...&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> ]
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>}
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/div>&lt;p>&lt;strong>Keys&lt;/strong>: SHA256 hash generated for the pdf file
&lt;strong>Values&lt;/strong>: list of file names that have this hash (meaning exactly same content)&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;em>Note:&lt;/em> Hash will be different even if only spacing changes in the pdf. &lt;strong>So it does not represent text.&lt;/strong>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Dataset Structure</title><link>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/dataset-structure/</link><pubDate>Fri, 04 Apr 2025 10:17:12 +0530</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/dataset-structure/</guid><description>&lt;h2 class="relative group">Initially provided dataset
&lt;div id="initially-provided-dataset" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700"
style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#initially-provided-dataset" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>
&lt;pre tabindex="0">&lt;code>├── 2024
│   ├── acts_07_12_2024_13_12_2024
│   ├── acts_14_12_2024_16_12_2024
│   ├── acts_17_12_2024_19_12_2024
│   ├── acts_20_12_2024_31_12_2024
│   ├── regulations_07_12_2024_13_12_2024
│   ├── regulations_14_12_2024_16_12_2024
│   ├── regulations_17_12_2024_19_12_2024
│   └── regulations_20_12_2024_31_12_2024
└── 2025
   ├── acts_01_01_2025
   └── regulations_01_01_2025
&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;p>Each folder here represents a version.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>For example, &lt;code>acts_07_12_2024_13_12_2024&lt;/code> is valid from 12th December 2024 to 13th December 2024. &lt;code>acts_01_01_2025&lt;/code> is valid from 1st January 2025 until the next version.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Knowledge Graph Implementation for Document Retrieval</title><link>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/knowledge-graph-implementation-for-document-retrieval/</link><pubDate>Mon, 31 Mar 2025 10:47:57 +0530</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/notes/konze-legal-ai/knowledge-graph-implementation-for-document-retrieval/</guid><description>&lt;h2 class="relative group">Overview
&lt;div id="overview" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100">
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700"
style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#overview" aria-label="Anchor">#&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Our system implements a graph-based approach to enhance document retrieval by leveraging the semantic connections between documents. Here&amp;rsquo;s how it works:&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 class="relative group">Graph Construction Phase
&lt;div id="graph-construction-phase" class="anchor">&lt;/div>
&lt;span
